  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">70 people showed up during a heatwave to build.

Last Saturday we hosted the <a class="link" href="https://de.linkedin.com/company/tech-europe-community?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>{Tech: Europe}</a> hackathon at our London office. It was incredible to see so many people building on top of Attio. 

The standout project was SellFast by <a class="link" href="https://uk.linkedin.com/in/yanhong-billy-zhao-9913ba140?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Yanhong (Billy) Zhao</a> and <a class="link" href="https://uk.linkedin.com/in/vincent-hao?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Vincent Hao</a>, who built a Pokémon battle sales training tool that pulls call recordings from Attio and uses voice agents to run live battles where reps face real customer questions.

They walked away with the Attio track and the overall win.

Congrats to every team that shipped something on the day. You set the bar for the next one.</p>
<!---->  </div>



        

        
            
      
    
    
    

